The runtime image is built on `cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base` (pinned by
digest in Dockerfile) plus ca-certificates, git and python-3.13 from Wolfi's
apk repositories; the :reachability variant adds go, nodejs and npm from the
same repositories. A `debian:bookworm-slim` stage is used at BUILD time only,
to run dpkg over the Syft and Grype .deb artifacts -- nothing from its
filesystem reaches either published image. These base packages carry their own
licenses (GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, LGPL, PSF-2.0, and others). The full composition of
the published image, including base-image packages, is enumerated in the SPDX
SBOM attached to each release as an OCI attestation -- see "Supply chain
security" in README.md for how to inspect it.
